Vercel Web Analytics Implementation Report
==========================================

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

Changes Made:
-------------

1. **Installed @vercel/analytics package** (v1.6.1)
   - Used npm install to add the package
   - Updated package.json with the new dependency
   - Updated package-lock.json with resolved dependencies

2. **Modified app/layout.tsx**
   - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
   - Added <Analytics /> component inside the <body> tag, after {children}
   - Preserved all existing code structure, imports, and styling

Implementation Details:
-----------------------

The Analytics component has been properly integrated into the root layout following Vercel's best practices for Next.js App Router projects:

- The component is placed at the end of the <body> tag to ensure it loads after the main content
- No configuration is required - the component will automatically track page views and web vitals
- The implementation is TypeScript-compatible and follows the existing code style

Verification:
-------------

- Linter was run: app/layout.tsx has no linting errors
- The changes introduce no new TypeScript errors
- Package installation completed successfully
- Lock files were properly updated

Note:
-----

The build process revealed pre-existing syntax errors in app/components/Projects.tsx (lines 10-14 have unquoted file paths that should be strings). These errors exist in the original codebase and are unrelated to the Analytics implementation. The Analytics integration itself is correct and will work properly once those pre-existing issues are resolved.

Next Steps:
-----------

Once deployed to Vercel, the Analytics dashboard will automatically start collecting data. No additional configuration is needed unless you want to enable specific features like custom events or audience tracking.
